The rootless Podman behind unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock was upgraded
during the #59 work: 5.4.2 (Debian /usr/bin/podman) -> 5.8.4 (~/.local/bin/podman
via a systemd override). Same socket path, newer binary.

MEASURED via GET /version through this client on 2026-08-27:

  Version:    5.8.4
  ApiVersion: 1.44          <- was 1.41
  Components: Podman Engine 5.8.4, Conmon 2.1.12, crun 1.21

The announced API version changed, which matters because negotiate_version
negotiates within whatever the daemon reports.

Every '5.4.2' and 'API 1.41' currently written down is correct for the old
measurements and stale as a description of this machine. It appears in:

  - CLAUDE.md ('announces API 1.41')
  - .claude/rules/api-docker-rules.md ('announces API 1.41')
  - the skill api-docker-core (Podman references)
  - tickets #45, #50, #52, #54, #59 and the POD that quotes their numbers
    (API::Docker::Error::HTTP names 'rootless Podman 5.4.2' for the kill
    message; Containers::attach and others quote 5.4.2)

Do NOT rewrite the old measurements to say 5.8.4 -- they were taken against
5.4.2 and that is what they measured. Rewrite only the sentences that describe
what is on this machine *now*, and leave each recorded measurement labelled with
the version it was taken against.

Re-verified on 5.8.4 during #59, still true:
  - attach to an exited container never closes (the #52 hang)
  - the full suite is green live, read-only and write

Not re-measured on 5.8.4: the #45 error-inside-a-200 shape, the #50 kill message
text, the #54 stats-on-exit behaviour.
